00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:59.000
But for African Americans, if you consider, in the 1970s, who have only been federally protected in a public accommodation like a restaurant for maybe five, 10 years, going to McDonald's is actually a really big deal. So when I started reading Dr. Chatlin's book, I think I was expecting kind of a takedown of McDonald's, kind of like fast food nation, just the knives out, talking about all the ways that fast food companies abuse workers and animals and the planet.
但对于非裔美国人来说，如果你考虑到在20世纪70年代，他们联邦保护的公共住宿权利（比如餐馆）也才刚刚获得大概五年、十年，去麦当劳其实是一件非常了不起的大事。所以当我开始阅读查特林博士的书时，我想我大概是期待对麦当劳的某种批判，有点像《快餐帝国》那种，直接亮出底牌，痛斥快餐公司盘剥工人和动物以及地球的种种行径。

